{"prompt_id": "oomkilled-confirm", "rep": 0, "prompt": "How do I confirm a pod was OOMKilled?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "seed"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers all key facts in the reference: describe showing Last State Terminated, Reason OOMKilled, Exit Code 137; the jsonpath for lastState.terminated.reason; and comparing kubectl top with the memory limit. Every claim, including the events command, the metrics-server requirement and the Evicted distinction, appears in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2906, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2906, "model": null, "output_tokens": 285, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 285, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.97, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3288, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3288, "model": null, "output_tokens": 139, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 139, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "answer": "Run `kubectl --context kind-qa -n qa describe pod <pod>`. An OOM kill shows as Last State: Terminated, Reason: OOMKilled, Exit Code: 137. You can also print the reason directly with `kubectl get pod <pod> -o jsonpath='{.status.containerStatuses[*].lastState.terminated.reason}'`, and check events with `get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp`. To see how close the pod is to its limit, compare `kubectl top pod <pod>` (current usage only, and it needs metrics-server) with the container's memory limit. Don't confuse this with eviction: pods evicted under node memory pressure show status `Evicted`, not `OOMKilled`."}}
{"prompt_id": "chaos-crash", "rep": 0, "prompt": "How many replies fail when an inference pod crashes?", "tags": ["resilience", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states all reference facts: 29-46 failed of about 540 replies, 91.6-94.6% availability, and back to 2 replicas in 1.8 s. Every claim, including the 0.2-0.3 s gap, the cause of the failures and the pass criteria (no failure once both replicas are ready, never 2 s without a successful reply, availability of at least 85%), is supported by the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3864, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3864, "model": null, "output_tokens": 234, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 234, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.93, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4155, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4155, "model": null, "output_tokens": 155, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 155, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "README#inference-performance", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "In typical results (kind on a laptop, six runs), a crash of one inference replica under 8 streaming users caused 29\u201346 failed replies out of about 540, for 91.6\u201394.6% availability. The longest gap with no successful reply was 0.2\u20130.3 s, and both replicas were ready again in 1.8 s. The failures are the replies being streamed at that moment, plus new requests that reach the dead pod in the second before its readiness probe fails. The test requires no failures once both replicas are ready again, never 2 s without a successful reply, and availability of at least 85%."}}
{"prompt_id": "latency-callout", "rep": 0, "prompt": "When does the KPI review call out a latency regression?", "tags": ["kpis", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states all key facts: TP99 more than 40% above the median of the last 8 merges, adjusted for whole-run slowdown, at least 2 ms worse, and a yellow callout that does not fail the build. Every claim, including the SLO-scenario condition, the 4\u21926 ms example and the callout placement, is supported by the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2526, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2526, "model": null, "output_tokens": 255, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 255, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 4.06, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2843, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2843, "model": null, "output_tokens": 135, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 135, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["KPIs#api-latency", "KPIs#tenets", "README#qa-kpis", "KPIs#review-cadence", "KPIs#what-fails-the-build-and-what-doesn-t"], "cited": ["KPIs#api-latency", "README#qa-kpis", "KPIs#what-fails-the-build-and-what-doesn-t"], "expected": ["KPIs#api-latency"], "answer": "A regression is called out for scenarios that have a latency SLO when TP99 is more than 40% above the median of the last 8 merges to main, and at least 2 ms worse. The 40% is measured after allowing for how much slower the whole run was (the median of every scenario's change), because a slow CI runner slows all scenarios together. The 2 ms floor keeps run-to-run noise on shared runners (e.g. a 4 \u2192 6 ms change, +50%) from being flagged. A regression is a yellow callout at the top of the review and does not fail the build; only a missed SLO does."}}
{"prompt_id": "inference-saturation", "rep": 0, "prompt": "At what number of concurrent users does the mock inference service saturate, and what happens?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer gives saturation at 32 users, throughput plateau (~1,267 tokens/s), TTFT TP99 821 ms, and queueing for the 16 batch slots, matching the reference. Every claim, including the 1,238 vs 1,267 comparison, 417 ms TP50, 19 ms between tokens and waiting rather than failing, appears in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4269, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4269, "model": null, "output_tokens": 235, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 235, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.95, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4617, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4617, "model": null, "output_tokens": 148, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 148, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#inference-performance", "README#performance-testing", "README#the-system-under-test", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#scope"], "cited": ["README#inference-performance"], "expected": ["README#inference-performance"], "answer": "The service saturates at 32 concurrent users. The mock generates 16 replies at once in a fixed batch. Up to 16 users, throughput grows almost linearly and TTFT stays flat. At 32 users throughput stops growing (1,238 tokens/s at 16 users vs. 1,267 at 32), and TTFT jumps 16\u00d7: TP50 is 417 ms and TP99 is 821 ms, because half the requests queue for a free slot. Time between tokens stays about the same (TP99 19 ms), so once a reply starts it streams just as smoothly. Requests past capacity wait rather than fail."}}
{"prompt_id": "pod-pending", "rep": 0, "prompt": "How do I debug a pod that stays in Pending?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "unanswerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": null, "cited_ok": null}, "explanation": {}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2957, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2957, "model": null, "output_tokens": 269, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 269, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.98, "judge_model": null, "judge_usage": null, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk"], "expected": [], "answer": "The documentation does not cover pods stuck in Pending. The Kubernetes runbook only deals with CrashLoopBackOff and OOMKilled. The closest it offers is three general first commands for any failing pod, run in the `qa` namespace with the `kind-qa` context: `get pods` to see the STATUS and RESTARTS columns, `describe pod <pod>` to see Last State, Reason, Exit Code and Events, and `logs <pod> --previous`. It gives no Pending-specific causes or fixes."}}
{"prompt_id": "oomkilled-confirm", "rep": 1, "prompt": "How do I confirm a pod was OOMKilled?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "seed"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: describe pod showing Last State Terminated, Reason OOMKilled, Exit Code 137; the jsonpath for lastState.terminated.reason; and comparing kubectl top usage with the memory limit. Each claim, including the events command, the metrics-server requirement and the eviction distinction, appears in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2906, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2906, "model": null, "output_tokens": 308, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 308, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 4.55, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3311, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3311, "model": null, "output_tokens": 142, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 142, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "answer": "Run `kubectl --context kind-qa -n qa describe pod <pod>` and look under Last State. An OOMKill shows as Terminated with Reason `OOMKilled` and Exit Code 137. You can read the reason directly with `kubectl --context kind-qa -n qa get pod <pod> -o jsonpath='{.status.containerStatuses[*].lastState.terminated.reason}'`, and check events with `get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp`. To see current memory, use `kubectl top pod <pod>` (needs metrics-server; it shows current usage only, not history) and compare it with the container's memory limit from `.spec.containers[*].resources.limits.memory`. Don't confuse this with an eviction, which shows status `Evicted`, not `OOMKilled`."}}
{"prompt_id": "crashloop-what-to-check", "rep": 2, "prompt": "What should I check when a pod is stuck in CrashLoopBackOff?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "seed"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: it is a symptom with growing back-off, the get pods, describe pod and logs --previous commands, reading the exit code, and all six common causes. Each claim, including the back-off timings, the exit code table and the get pods -w check, appears in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2913, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2913, "model": null, "output_tokens": 487, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 487, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 5.65, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3486, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3486, "model": null, "output_tokens": 118, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 118, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod"], "answer": "CrashLoopBackOff is a symptom, not a cause: the container keeps exiting and the kubelet waits longer between restarts (10 s, 20 s, 40 s\u2026, capped at 5 minutes). Start with the three commands: `kubectl --context kind-qa -n qa get pods` (STATUS and RESTARTS), `describe pod <pod>` (Last State, Reason, Exit Code, Events), and `logs <pod> --previous`, because the log without `--previous` shows the new container, not the one that died. Read the exit code under Last State: 1 means the app failed (an exception or bad config), 137 means SIGKILL (usually OOMKilled, or a failed liveness probe), 139 is a segfault and 143 is SIGTERM. Then match the cause: a missing or wrong Secret/ConfigMap/env var, a wrong command or image (exit 1 or 127, \"not found\"), an unreachable dependency, a failing liveness probe (consider a `startupProbe`), OOMKilled, or permission errors from a read-only filesystem or `securityContext`. After the fix, run `kubectl get pods -w` and check that the RESTARTS count stops growing."}}
{"prompt_id": "crashloop-what-to-check", "rep": 0, "prompt": "What should I check when a pod is stuck in CrashLoopBackOff?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "seed"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: it is a symptom, the three commands (including Last State, Reason, Exit Code, Events and --previous), reading the exit code, and the common causes (config/Secret, wrong command or image, dependency, liveness probe, OOM, permissions). Each claim, including the back-off timings, exit codes, and the after-the-fix steps, is supported by the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2913, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2913, "model": null, "output_tokens": 462, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 462, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 5.84, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3461, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3461, "model": null, "output_tokens": 154, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 154, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod"], "answer": "CrashLoopBackOff is a symptom: the container keeps exiting and the kubelet backs off between restarts (10 s, 20 s, 40 s\u2026, capped at 5 minutes). Run `kubectl --context kind-qa -n qa get pods` (STATUS/RESTARTS), `describe pod <pod>` (Last State, Reason, Exit Code, Events) and `logs <pod> --previous` (log of the container that just died; without `--previous` you see the new one). Read the exit code: 1 = application failure (startup exception, bad config), 137 = SIGKILL (usually OOMKilled or a failed liveness probe), 139 = segfault, 143 = SIGTERM; 127/\"not found\" points to a wrong command or image. Also check for missing Secrets/ConfigMaps, unreachable dependencies, `Liveness probe failed` events (fix the probe or add a `startupProbe`) and permission-denied errors (check `securityContext`). After the fix, watch with `kubectl get pods -w` until RESTARTS stops growing, and record the cause and fix in the ticket."}}
{"prompt_id": "crashloop-what-to-check", "rep": 1, "prompt": "What should I check when a pod is stuck in CrashLoopBackOff?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "seed"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 0.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: the symptom meaning, the three commands, reading the exit code, and all the common causes. One claim is not supported by the excerpts: it lists exit code 127 as 'wrong command' alone, while the excerpts say 'exit code 1 or 127' for a wrong command or image. Everything else matches the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2913, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2913, "model": null, "output_tokens": 500, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 500, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 6.37, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3494, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3494, "model": null, "output_tokens": 138, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 138, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod"], "answer": "Start with three commands: `kubectl --context kind-qa -n qa get pods` (look at STATUS and RESTARTS), `kubectl ... describe pod <pod>` (Last State, Reason, Exit Code, Events), and `kubectl ... logs <pod> --previous`. Use `--previous` because a plain `logs` shows the new container, which often hasn't failed yet. CrashLoopBackOff is only a symptom: Kubernetes keeps restarting the container and waits longer each time (10 s, 20 s, 40 s and so on, up to 5 minutes). The exit code under Last State points to the cause:\n- 1: the application failed, for example a startup exception or bad config.\n- 127: wrong command.\n- 137: SIGKILL, usually OOMKilled or a failed liveness probe.\n- 139: segfault.\n- 143: SIGTERM.\nCommon causes are missing or wrong config (Secret/ConfigMap), a wrong command or image, an unreachable dependency, a failing liveness probe, running out of memory, or permission problems (read-only filesystem or non-root user). After the fix, run `kubectl get pods -w` and confirm the RESTARTS count stops growing."}}
{"prompt_id": "exit-code-137", "rep": 0, "prompt": "What does exit code 137 usually mean for a container?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states SIGKILL, most often OOMKilled, or killed after a failed liveness probe, matching the reference. Every claim (memory limit exceeded, kernel kill with no graceful shutdown, describe Last State showing OOMKilled and 137) is supported by the runbook excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3700, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3700, "model": null, "output_tokens": 196, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 196, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.17, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3927, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3927, "model": null, "output_tokens": 121, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 121, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#exit-criteria-testing-is-done"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "answer": "Exit code 137 means the container was killed with SIGKILL. Most often this is OOMKilled: the container used more memory than its memory limit and the kernel killed it at once, with no graceful shutdown. Less often, it was killed after a failed liveness probe. To confirm OOMKilled, look in `kubectl describe pod` under Last State for Reason `OOMKilled` and Exit Code 137."}}
