{"prompt_id": "backoff-timing", "rep": 1, "prompt": "How long does Kubernetes wait between restarts of a crash-looping container?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states the 10 s, 20 s, 40 s progression capped at 5 minutes, matching the reference. Every claim, including that the wait is what CrashLoopBackOff shows and that it is a symptom rather than a cause, appears in the runbook excerpt."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3656, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3656, "model": null, "output_tokens": 143, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 143, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.33, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3855, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3855, "model": null, "output_tokens": 111, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 111, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#first-three-commands-for-any-failing-pod", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "answer": "The wait grows after each crash: the kubelet waits 10 s, then 20 s, then 40 s and so on, capped at 5 minutes. This waiting period is what the `CrashLoopBackOff` status shows. It is a symptom, not a cause: the cause is whatever makes the container exit."}}
