{"prompt_id": "verify-fix", "rep": 1, "prompt": "After fixing a crash loop, how do I know the fix worked?", "tags": ["k8s-runbook", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states both key facts: watch with `kubectl get pods -w` until RESTARTS stops growing, and for OOMKilled compare memory under load before and after. The extra advice about writing down the cause and fix, and the note that one quiet minute proves little, both appear in the 'After the fix' excerpt."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3541, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3541, "model": null, "output_tokens": 154, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 154, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.76, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3766, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3766, "model": null, "output_tokens": 123, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 123, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "answer": "Watch the pod for a while with `kubectl get pods -w`; the RESTARTS count must stop growing. If the crash loop was caused by OOMKilled, compare memory under load before and after the change, because one quiet minute proves little. The runbook also says to write down the cause and the fix in the ticket so the next on-call engineer finds it."}}
