x", "K8S_RUNBOOK#kubernetes-troubleshooting-runbook-crashloopbackoff-and-oomk", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "cited": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#after-the-fix"], "answer": "Watch the pod for a while with `kubectl get pods -w`; the RESTARTS count must stop growing. If the problem was OOMKilled, compare memory usage under load before and after the change, because one quiet minute proves little. Then record the cause and the fix in the ticket so the next on-call engineer can find it."}}
