{"prompt_id": "chaos-graceful", "rep": 0, "prompt": "What happens to users when an inference pod is stopped gracefully during the chaos test?", "tags": ["resilience", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: about 490 replies with 0 failed, 100% availability, preStop letting open streams finish, and recovery to 2 replicas in 1.3\u20131.6 s. Every claim, including the 0.2 s gap and the 5 of 485 failures without preStop, is stated in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3922, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3922, "model": null, "output_tokens": 239, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 239, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.38, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4237, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4237, "model": null, "output_tokens": 131, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 131, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#run-on-kubernetes", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "In the graceful case (a rolling update or node drain), the pod is deleted. Kubernetes stops routing to it, a `preStop` pause lets its open streams finish, and then it gets `SIGTERM`. The test requires not a single failed reply. In typical runs, about 490 replies all succeeded: 0 failed, 100% availability, a longest gap of 0.2 s with no successful reply, and both replicas back within 1.3\u20131.6 s. This works only because of `preStop`: in one run without the pause, 5 of 485 replies failed because streams were cut mid-reply."}}
