: "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#run-on-kubernetes", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "In the graceful case (like a rolling update or node drain), the pod is deleted. Kubernetes stops routing to it, a `preStop` pause lets its open streams finish, and only then is `SIGTERM` sent. The requirement is that not a single reply fails, and typical results meet it: about 490 replies, 0 failed, 100% availability, a longest gap of 0.2 s, and back to 2 replicas in 1.3\u20131.6 s. Without the `preStop` pause, one run failed 5 of 485 replies because streams were cut mid-reply."}}
