"retrieved": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#run-on-kubernetes", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "In the graceful case (a rolling update or node drain), the pod is deleted. Kubernetes stops routing to it, the `preStop` pause lets its open streams finish, and then it gets `SIGTERM`. Users see not a single failed reply. In typical runs that was ~490 replies, 0 failed, 100% availability, a longest gap of 0.2 s with no successful reply, and two replicas back in 1.3\u20131.6 s. This works only because of `preStop`: in one run without the pause, 5 of 485 replies failed because streams were cut mid-reply."}}
