ence-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2", "README#run-on-kubernetes", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "K8S_RUNBOOK#oomkilled"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "When a pod is deleted, Kubernetes removes it from the Service and signals the container at the same moment. The `preStop` pause lets the pod's open streams finish before `SIGTERM` arrives. In one run without the pause, the graceful stop failed 5 of 485 replies because streams were cut mid-reply; with it, none failed. Likewise, when `preStop` was removed in the rolling-upgrade test, the good-version release failed 28 of 282 replies."}}
