{"prompt_id": "chaos-crash", "rep": 2, "prompt": "How many replies fail when an inference pod crashes?", "tags": ["resilience", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer gives 29-46 failed of about 540 replies, availability 91.6-94.6%, and back to 2 replicas in 1.8 s, matching the reference. Every claim, including the failure causes and the test thresholds, is stated in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3864, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3864, "model": null, "output_tokens": 252, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 252, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.56, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4173, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4173, "model": null, "output_tokens": 107, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 107, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "README#inference-performance", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "In the crash scenario (`POST /debug/crash` kills the server, Kubernetes restarts the container), typical runs on kind on a laptop had about 540 replies with 29\u201346 failed. Availability was 91.6\u201394.6%, and the longest gap with no successful reply was 0.2\u20130.3 s. Both replicas were back in 1.8 s. The failures are the replies being streamed at the moment of the crash, plus new requests that reach the dead pod in the second before its readiness probe fails. The test requires no failures once both replicas are ready again, no 2 s gap without a successful reply, and availability of at least 85%."}}
