der-load", "README#inference-performance", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2"], "cited": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "expected": ["README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load"], "answer": "In typical results (kind on a laptop, six runs), a crash of one inference replica caused 29\u201346 failed replies out of about 540, giving 91.6\u201394.6% availability. The failures are the replies being streamed at that moment, plus new requests that reach the dead pod in the second before its readiness probe fails. The other replica keeps answering throughout, with the longest gap without a successful reply at 0.2\u20130.3 s. The test requires no failures once both replicas are ready again, never a 2 s gap without a successful reply, and availability of at least 85%."}}
{"prompt_id": "upgrade-broken", "rep": 0, "prompt": "What happens in the rolling-upgrade test when the new version is broken?", "tags": ["resilience", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states all reference facts: pods crash and never become ready, ProgressDeadlineExceeded after 30 s, rollback, zero failed replies, and two replicas available throughout. Every claim, including the typical results, the `kubectl rollout undo` comparison and the readiness probe with `maxUnavailable: 0`, is stated in the README and runbook excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3149, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3149, "model": null, "output_tokens": 306, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 306, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.54, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3498, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3498, "model": null, "output_tokens": 145, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 145, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2", "K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "TEST_PLAN#risks"], "cited": ["README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2", "K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load"], "answer": "The new pods crash at start, so they never become ready and receive no traffic. The Deployment reports `ProgressDeadlineExceeded` after 30 s, and the test then rolls back the way `kubectl rollout undo` does. The test requires that not a single reply fails, that no replies come from the broken version, and that two replicas stay available throughout. Typical results were 1,760\u20131,784 replies with 0 failed, a longest gap of 0.2 s, and 30.6\u201331.3 s total, with detection at 30.3\u201331.1 s. This works because of the readiness probe and `maxUnavailable: 0`, so a broken version costs a stalled rollout, not an outage."}}
