speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load-p2", "K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "TEST_PLAN#risks"], "cited": ["README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load", "K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff"], "expected": ["K8S_RUNBOOK#crashloopbackoff", "README#rolling-upgrades-releasing-under-load"], "answer": "The new pods crash at start, so they never become ready and get no traffic. After 30 s the Deployment reports `ProgressDeadlineExceeded`, and the test rolls back, as `kubectl rollout undo` does. It must hold that not a single reply fails, none come from the broken version, and two replicas stay available throughout. Typical runs had 1,760\u20131,784 replies with 0 failed, a longest gap of 0.2 s, and took 30.6\u201331.3 s, with the failure detected at 30.3\u201331.1 s. This works because of the readiness probe and `maxUnavailable: 0`. With `maxSurge: 0`, `maxUnavailable: 1`, the test fails because only 1 of 2 replicas is available."}}
