{"prompt_id": "aws-oidc", "rep": 0, "prompt": "How does the AWS QA environment avoid storing AWS keys in GitHub?", "tags": ["aws", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: OIDC short-lived credentials, the role trusting only main of this repository, and matching the immutable subject (owner and repository IDs). The extra details about the one-time setup and the repository variables are stated in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4682, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4682, "model": null, "output_tokens": 221, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 221, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.18, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4992, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4992, "model": null, "output_tokens": 107, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 107, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#aws-qa-environment", "README#run-against-a-qa-server", "README#project-layout", "README#what-this-demonstrates", "README#ci-cd-github-actions"], "cited": ["README#aws-qa-environment"], "expected": ["README#aws-qa-environment"], "answer": "CI doesn't use stored AWS keys. It signs in with GitHub's OIDC token to get short-lived credentials. The role, defined in `infra/aws-setup.yml`, trusts only `main` of this repository, so pull requests and forks can't use it. The role also matches GitHub's immutable subject (owner and repository IDs), so a recreated repository with the same name can't use it either. After a one-time setup, the stack's outputs are saved as the repository variables `AWS_ROLE_ARN` and `AWS_REGION`; without them the job is skipped."}}
