E#run-against-a-qa-server", "README#project-layout", "README#what-this-demonstrates", "README#ci-cd-github-actions"], "cited": ["README#aws-qa-environment"], "expected": ["README#aws-qa-environment"], "answer": "CI doesn't store AWS keys. It signs in with GitHub's OIDC token and gets short-lived credentials instead. The role it assumes is defined in `infra/aws-setup.yml` and trusts only `main` of this repository, so pull requests and forks can't use it. The role also matches GitHub's immutable subject (owner and repository IDs), so a recreated repository with the same name can't assume it. Its permissions are limited to creating and deleting `qa-env-*` stacks, launching only `t2/t3.micro` instances in one region, and deleting only resources tagged `project=qa-env`."}}
