 {"retrieved": ["README#aws-qa-environment", "README#run-against-a-qa-server", "README#project-layout", "README#what-this-demonstrates", "README#ci-cd-github-actions"], "cited": ["README#aws-qa-environment"], "expected": ["README#aws-qa-environment"], "answer": "CI doesn't store AWS keys in GitHub at all. It signs in with GitHub's OIDC token to get short-lived credentials. The role, defined in `infra/aws-setup.yml`, trusts only `main` of this repository, so pull requests and forks can't use it. It also matches GitHub's immutable subject (owner and repository IDs), so a recreated repository with the same name can't use it either. The only things saved in GitHub are the setup stack's outputs, as repository variables `AWS_ROLE_ARN` and `AWS_REGION`; without them the job is skipped."}}
