{"prompt_id": "docker-build-flag", "rep": 1, "prompt": "Why do the docker compose commands use --build?", "tags": ["docker-db", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states all key facts in the reference: code is copied at build time, Compose reuses existing images so a run without --build tests old code, and Docker rebuilds only what changed. The extra detail about cached layers, browsers and pip install rerunning only when requirements.txt changes is stated in the excerpt, so every claim is supported."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4070, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4070, "model": null, "output_tokens": 139, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 139, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.49, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4280, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4280, "model": null, "output_tokens": 128, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 128, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#or-in-docker-nothing-to-install-but-docker", "README#run-against-a-qa-server", "README#the-database-postgres-in-docker", "README#ci-cd-github-actions", "README#run-on-kubernetes"], "cited": ["README#or-in-docker-nothing-to-install-but-docker"], "expected": ["README#or-in-docker-nothing-to-install-but-docker"], "answer": "The code is copied into the images when they are built, and Compose reuses an existing image. Without `--build`, a run after a code change would test the old code. With it, Docker rebuilds only what changed using cached layers. So the browsers and `pip install` rerun only when `requirements.txt` changes."}}
