{"prompt_id": "db-race", "rep": 0, "prompt": "How does the database test for duplicate emails work, and how was it shown to be effective?", "tags": ["docker-db", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states every key fact in the reference: 10 simultaneous sign-ups with one email, one 201 and nine 409, the unique index on lower(email), and all 10 succeeding without the index so the test failed. Each claim, including the `tests/db` location and `db` marker, is supported by the database tests excerpt."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2723, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2723, "model": null, "output_tokens": 190, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 190, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.92, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2999, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2999, "model": null, "output_tokens": 125, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 125, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#performance-testing-p2", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#the-database-postgres-in-docker-p2", "TEST_PLAN#entry-criteria-testing-can-start", "README#how-the-requirements-are-covered"], "cited": ["README#the-database-postgres-in-docker-p2"], "expected": ["README#the-database-postgres-in-docker-p2"], "answer": "The database test (in `tests/db`, marker `db`) sends 10 sign-ups with the same email at the same moment and expects exactly one 201 and nine 409s. It targets a check-then-insert race that only the database's unique index on `lower(email)` can prevent. To show the test works, it was broken on purpose: with the unique index removed, all 10 sign-ups succeeded and the test failed. With the index in place, exactly one sign-up succeeds."}}
