"README#performance-testing-p2", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios", "README#the-database-postgres-in-docker-p2", "TEST_PLAN#entry-criteria-testing-can-start", "README#how-the-requirements-are-covered"], "cited": ["README#the-database-postgres-in-docker-p2", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios"], "expected": ["README#the-database-postgres-in-docker-p2"], "answer": "The database test fires 10 sign-ups with the same email at the same moment and expects exactly one 201 and nine 409s. It targets a check-then-insert race, which only the database's unique index on `lower(email)` prevents. Its effectiveness was shown by breaking it on purpose: without the unique index all 10 sign-ups succeeded and the test failed, and with the index exactly one succeeds."}}
