{"prompt_id": "login-many-users", "rep": 0, "prompt": "Why does the login load test log in as 200 different users instead of one?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers all key facts in the reference: the cache effect, per-user rate limits or lockout, and the login_users fixture creating users and keys with the admin key before timing starts. Every claim, including the extra token-ownership check and cleanup, is stated in the README excerpt."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4271, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4271, "model": null, "output_tokens": 179, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 179, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.27, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4541, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4541, "model": null, "output_tokens": 112, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 112, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#performance-testing", "README#the-system-under-test", "README#design-decisions", "README#design-decisions-p2", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios"], "cited": ["README#performance-testing"], "expected": ["README#performance-testing"], "answer": "Logging in 200 times as one user mostly measures a cache, and in a real system it would run into per-user rate limits or account lockout. With separate users, the scenario also checks that each token belongs to its own user: it can read its own user's transactions (200) and is refused the next user's (403). The `login_users` fixture uses the admin key to create the users and their keys (`POST /api/users/:id/api-keys`) before timing starts, and deletes them afterwards."}}
