ed": ["README#performance-testing", "README#the-system-under-test", "README#design-decisions", "README#design-decisions-p2", "TEST_PLAN#scenarios"], "cited": ["README#performance-testing"], "expected": ["README#performance-testing"], "answer": "Logging in as one user 200 times mostly measures a cache, and in a real system it would hit per-user rate limits or account lockout. The \"login, different users\" scenario therefore uses 200 users, each with its own API key, at 10 parallel. It also checks that each token belongs to its user: the token can read its own user's transactions (200) and is refused the next user's (403). The `login_users` fixture uses the admin key to create the users and their keys via `POST /api/users/:id/api-keys` before timing starts, and deletes them afterwards."}}
{"prompt_id": "inference-saturation", "rep": 1, "prompt": "At what number of concurrent users does the mock inference service saturate, and what happens?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer covers every key fact in the reference: saturation at 32 users, throughput flat at about 1,267 tokens/s, TTFT TP99 821 ms, and queueing for the 16 batch slots. Every claim, including the 417 ms TP50, the 16\u00d7 jump, 19 ms between tokens and requests waiting rather than failing, appears in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4269, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4269, "model": null, "output_tokens": 237, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 237, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.23, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4619, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4619, "model": null, "output_tokens": 144, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 144, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#inference-performance", "README#performance-testing", "README#the-system-under-test", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#scope"], "cited": ["README#inference-performance"], "expected": ["README#inference-performance"], "answer": "In the laptop run, the mock saturates at 32 concurrent users. It generates replies in a fixed batch of 16, so up to 16 users throughput grows almost linearly (1,238 tokens/s) while TTFT stays flat. At 32 users throughput stops growing (1,267 tokens/s, saturated) and TTFT jumps 16\u00d7, with TP50 at 417 ms and TP99 at 821 ms, because half the requests queue for a free slot. Once a reply starts, it streams just as smoothly: time-between-tokens TP99 is still 19 ms. Requests past capacity wait rather than fail."}}
{"prompt_id": "inference-saturation", "rep": 2, "prompt": "At what number of concurrent users does the mock inference service saturate, and what happens?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer gives 32 users, throughput plateau (~1,267 tokens/s), TTFT TP99 821 ms, and queueing for the 16 batch slots, matching the reference. Every claim, including the 51 ms, 417 ms, 19 ms and 18 ms figures and the 16\u00d7 jump, appears in the excerpts."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4269, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4269, "model": null, "output_tokens": 239, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 239, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 3.24, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4621, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4621, "model": null, "output_tokens": 133, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 133, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#inference-performance", "README#performance-testing", "README#the-system-under-test", "README#chaos-testing-losing-an-inference-pod-under-load", "TEST_PLAN#scope"], "cited": ["README#inference-performance"], "expected": ["README#inference-performance"], "answer": "The mock saturates at 32 concurrent users. It works like a model server with a fixed batch of 16 replies at once, so up to 16 users throughput grows almost linearly and TTFT stays flat (TTFT TP99 51 ms at 16 users). At 32 users, throughput stops growing (1,267 vs 1,238 tokens/s) and TTFT jumps 16\u00d7: TP50 is 417 ms and TP99 is 821 ms, because half the requests queue for a free slot. Once a reply starts, it still streams smoothly: time between tokens TP99 is 19 ms, against 18 ms at 16 users."}}
{"prompt_id": "ttft-slo", "rep": 2, "prompt": "What is TTFT and what is its SLO in this project?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states TTFT is time to first token (how long a user stares at a blank screen) and that its SLO is TP99 \u2264 250 ms, up to capacity, matching the reference. The extra details (run_stream_load, the endpoint, and the 50 ms time-between-tokens SLO) are all stated in the README excerpt."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3903, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3903, "model": null, "output_tokens": 190, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 190, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.37, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4167, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4167, "model": null, "output_tokens": 131, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 131, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#inference-performance", "KPIs#output-metrics-what-customers-feel", "KPIs#api-latency", "README#performance-testing", "README#qa-kpis"], "cited": ["README#inference-performance"], "expected": ["README#inference-performance"], "answer": "TTFT (time to first token) measures how long a user stares at a blank screen before an LLM streaming reply begins. Its SLO in this project is TP99 \u2264 250 ms, up to capacity. It is measured by `run_stream_load` in `utils/load.py` against the mock's OpenAI-compatible `POST /v1/chat/completions` endpoint. It is tracked separately from time between tokens, which has a TP99 \u2264 50 ms SLO at any load."}}
