["README#inference-performance", "KPIs#output-metrics-what-customers-feel", "KPIs#api-latency", "README#performance-testing", "README#qa-kpis"], "cited": ["README#inference-performance"], "expected": ["README#inference-performance"], "answer": "TTFT is time to first token: it tells you how long a user stares at a blank screen before a streamed LLM reply starts. Its SLO is TP99 \u2264 250 ms, up to capacity. `test_chat_streaming_under_load` checks it across 1, 8, 16 and 32 concurrent users against the mock's streaming chat endpoint. In the example laptop run, TTFT TP99 was 32\u201351 ms up to 16 users, then jumped to 821 ms at 32 users, where requests queue for a free slot."}}
{"prompt_id": "ttft-slo", "rep": 1, "prompt": "What is TTFT and what is its SLO in this project?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer defines TTFT as time to first token (a user staring at a blank screen) and gives the SLO as TP99 \u2264 250 ms up to capacity, matching the reference. The extra details (time between tokens SLO of 50 ms, 51 ms TP99 at 16 users, 821 ms at 32 users, 16-reply batch) all appear in the README excerpt."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3903, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3903, "model": null, "output_tokens": 207, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 207, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.6, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4184, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 4184, "model": null, "output_tokens": 147, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 147, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#inference-performance", "KPIs#output-metrics-what-customers-feel", "KPIs#api-latency", "README#performance-testing", "README#qa-kpis"], "cited": ["README#inference-performance"], "expected": ["README#inference-performance"], "answer": "TTFT is time to first token: in LLM inference testing it measures how long a user stares at a blank screen before the first token of a streamed reply arrives. Its SLO is TP99 \u2264 250 ms, up to capacity. It is measured separately from time between tokens (SLO TP99 \u2264 50 ms at any load). In the laptop run, TTFT stayed flat up to 16 users (TP99 51 ms) but jumped to a TP99 of 821 ms at 32 users once the 16-reply batch was saturated."}}
{"prompt_id": "perf-not-parallel", "rep": 1, "prompt": "Why aren't the load tests run in parallel with pytest-xdist?", "tags": ["performance", "answerable", "drafted"], "status": "ok", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "grade": {"correct": 1.0, "grounded": 1.0, "abstain_ok": 1.0, "retrieval_hit": 1.0, "cited_ok": 1.0}, "explanation": {"correct": "The answer states both key facts from the reference: workers compete for the CPU and distort latency, and the perf fixture skips load tests inside a worker so `pytest -m perf` stays a single process. Every claim appears in the README's parallel-runs section."}, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3488, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3488, "model": null, "output_tokens": 110, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 110, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "latency_s": 2.41, "judge_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "judge_usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3679, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 3679, "model": null, "output_tokens": 102, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 102, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "meta": {"retrieved": ["README#design-decisions-p2", "README#ci-cd-github-actions-p2", "README#quick-start", "README#performance-testing-p2", "README#finpay-qa-automation-framework"], "cited": ["README#design-decisions-p2"], "expected": ["README#design-decisions-p2"], "answer": "Load tests never run in parallel because the xdist workers would compete for the CPU and distort each other's latency measurements. To prevent this, the perf fixture skips them inside a worker, so `pytest -m perf` stays a single process."}}
