d", "README#design-decisions", "README#how-the-requirements-are-covered", "README#project-layout", "README#what-i-d-add-with-more-time"], "cited": ["README#project-layout", "README#how-the-requirements-are-covered"], "expected": ["README#how-the-requirements-are-covered", "README#project-layout"], "answer": "There are 76 data-driven negative test cases. They live in `data/negative/*.json`, spread across 5 files covering users, user updates, transactions, API keys and auth headers, and each case records the expected error. They are loaded by `utils/test_data.py` and run by `tests/api/test_negative_data.py`, one run per case."}}
