"meta": {"retrieved": ["README#design-decisions-p2", "README#ci-cd-github-actions-p2", "README#quick-start", "README#performance-testing-p2", "README#finpay-qa-automation-framework"], "cited": ["README#design-decisions-p2"], "expected": ["README#design-decisions-p2"], "answer": "Load tests never run in parallel because the xdist workers would compete for the CPU and distort each other's latency measurements. To enforce this, the perf fixture skips the load tests inside a worker, so `pytest -m perf` always stays a single process. By contrast, the functional tests do use `-n auto` in CI and Docker (124 tests take 3.9 s in one process and 2.3 s in parallel on an 8-core laptop)."}}
