, "README#performance-testing-p2", "README#finpay-qa-automation-framework"], "cited": ["README#design-decisions-p2"], "expected": ["README#design-decisions-p2"], "answer": "Load tests are kept out of parallel runs because xdist workers would compete for the CPU and distort each other's latency measurements. To prevent this, the perf fixture skips load tests when they run inside an xdist worker, so `pytest -m perf` always stays a single process."}}
