 "README#finpay-qa-automation-framework", "README#ci-cd-github-actions-p2", "README#what-i-d-add-with-more-time", "README#project-layout"], "cited": ["README#ci-cd-github-actions", "README#ci-cd-github-actions-p2"], "expected": ["README#ci-cd-github-actions-p2"], "answer": "On a pull request, the performance tests (`docker compose run --rm tests pytest -m perf`) run only if the API + UI tests job passed, and only if a performance-relevant file changed. That means the server code (`mock_server/*.py`), `tests/perf/`, `utils/`, test setup (`conftest.py`, `config.py`, `pytest.ini`), `requirements.txt`, or the workflow. A README or `.gitignore` edit runs only the API + UI tests. On a PR they run at normal load (`PERF_LOAD=1`) as a quick pre-merge check, while merges to `main` use 3\u00d7 load. Manual runs always include them."}}
